{
  "task": "M-05-B.2 constrained groups and consumer resolution domains",
  "status": "unreviewed_candidate",
  "acceptance_owner": "Root",
  "implementation": [
    "Core constrained wrapper defines four cardinalities, positive local member/group guards, guard DAG validation, explicit defaults, Omitted/Explicit and Additive/Exact intent.",
    "Owner edges compose accepted DefinitionId/optional LockId/TargetInstanceId, LockTargetRole and DependencyRole with explicit resolution domain, instance/configuration and package identity. Native version text is retained without SemVer conversion.",
    "Generated epoch-1 request/result and wire-owned semantic admission feed public pure features::configuration::resolve_consumer_configuration. Source definitions are supplied explicitly; selected features feed the existing B1 evaluator.",
    "Separate domains resolve independently, shared instance requests union, exact conflicts retain both consumer edges, dormant group/member intent is retained until guards activate. Defaults require explicit UseDeclaredDefaults policy. NeedsSelection yields no expansion or writes.",
    "Existing authored TOML features/requires grammar and B1 APIs remain unchanged. Permanent PROP003 additions preserve all prior lines."
  ],
  "criterion_dispositions": [
    {
      "statement": "Generated requests retain owner edge/domain/target and choice provenance.",
